Under Agent Studio, you can mainly build, configure, test, and manage AI agents.

🤖 What can we perform in Agent Studio?

Create AI Agents
Build an agent for a specific task.
Example: Customer Support Agent, Travel Agent, Restaurant Agent.
-----------

Choose an AI Model
Select models such as Gemini and other available models.
The model acts as the agent's "brain."

-------------

Give the Agent Instructions
Define what the agent should do and how it should behave.

Example:

"You are a travel assistant. Help users plan trips within their budget."

--------------

Connect Tools

Give the agent tools it can use to perform actions.

For example:

Agent
  ↓
Search Tool
  ↓
Database
  ↓
API

------------

Connect Data / Knowledge

Give the agent access to documents or other information.

This is useful for RAG applications.

=========

Test the Agent
Chat with the agent directly in Studio.
Try different questions and see how it responds.

=============

Build Agent Workflows
Define how the agent should reason, use tools, retrieve information, and respond.

============

Deploy the Agent
Once the agent works correctly, you can make it available for an application or users.

=========

Simple example

Suppose you create a Travel Agent:

                 👤 User
                    ↓
              🤖 Travel Agent
                    ↓
              🧠 Gemini Model
                    ↓
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       ↓            ↓            ↓
   Hotel Tool    Flight Tool   Weather
       ↓            ↓            ↓
       └────────────┼────────────┘
                    ↓
             ✈️ Travel Plan

The important difference from your previous Cloud Shell exercise is:

=========

Cloud Shell: You write Python code to tell Gemini what to do.

Agent Studio: You can design an agent, give it instructions, connect models/tools/data, test it, and manage its workflow through the Google Cloud environment.

For your AI Agent + RAG + MCP learning, Agent Studio is especially useful for understanding how a basic Gemini model becomes an AI agent that can use tools and data to accomplish a task.

